  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When a custom property is used directly as the `maxDistance` argument of `Physics.Raycast`, the method returns `true`, but `hit.collider` is `null`.\n\nAssigning the property value to a local `float` before the call avoids the issue. Both versions cast the same ray against the same Collider, so they should return the same `RaycastHit`.\n\nThe issue occurs with both auto-properties (`{ get; private set; }`) and non-serialized getter-only properties.\n\nA property getter appearing after an `out` argument may be related, but I have not confirmed the exact trigger.\n\nThe full reproduction code is attached as a screenshot.",
